{"description":"M4 — the retrieval surface stays bounded and does not grow. eka context remains one door, gaining --for; the MCP surface continues the grouping the internal research already designed (25 flat tools to roughly six read/write/ops handles with verbatim sub-capability descriptions), and no twenty-sixth tool is added without retiring one. The measured cost is the reason: 25 tool schemas are roughly 6 to 12 thousand tokens per session, against an AWS-published 250-500 tokens per tool schema and coarse per-workflow tool design.","acceptanceCriteria":"- The grouped MCP surface is exposed as designed, with each group description naming its sub-capabilities verbatim so discovery does not regress, and existing tool names preserved as aliases where a consumer may depend on them.\n- A test asserts the tool count and the schema byte cost, so the surface cannot grow silently: adding a tool without retiring one fails.\n- The prefix cost of the tool surface is measured before and after, recorded as numbers rather than an estimate.\n- Any new tool proposal in this wave is closed as part of a retirement, not as an addition."}